+// MLB Power Pros 2008 (RL8E54): a native MIXUpdateSettings (0x800BFB24, the AX MIX library),
+// 1.8% of the Switch main thread in the stock match profile (run 3), plus the 1.1% of its
+// per-voice callee __MIXRmtUpdateSettings (0x800C1264).
+//
+// Who calls it: the game's sound engine thread (0x80027A54), woken every 5 ms by its ticker
+// thread (0x80027BF8, OSSleepTicks), walks its 55 channels (0x8002D768) and calls
+// MIXUpdateSettings once per channel that starts or fades, after each MIXSetFader; every call
+// walks all AX voices (r13-27104) and calls __MIXRmtUpdateSettings for each one that has a
+// voice. The AX user frame callback (0x80027BF4) is an empty blr. All of it is guest-thread code
+// (fibers on the main thread), as the single Broadway core ran it on the Wii: the per-frame
+// cost is the game's own, not an HLE artefact.
+//
+// The translation spends most of that time on the call boundary: one InvokeDirectCpu with a
+// full register sync, a guest stack frame and the spills around it per voice, and CR0/XER
+// bookkeeping at every compare. This is the same instruction sequence with __MIXRmtUpdateSettings
+// and its __MIXGetVolume calls (0x800BE098) inlined, guest registers as locals, CR0 kept as the
+// last compare's three flags and XER[CA] as one bit.
+//
+// Kept exactly, also for the volatile registers (cross-checked against the translation in
+// qemu-aarch64, see below): every guest load and store in program order (stack frames included,
+// the epilogues read r26-r31, r30/r31 and LR back from the stack as the original does), the
+// MMIO write policy of each store (the translation's one ResolveRangeHost group, the 15 remote
+// speaker halfwords at AXVPB+0x104, is resolved the same way), r0 r1 r3-r9 r11 r26-r31, CR0,
+// XER[CA] and LR as the translation leaves them; r10, r12, CR1-7, CTR and the FPRs untouched.
+// The checked access mode (no flat view) runs the translation itself, which
+// REGISTER_NATIVE_FUNCTION_AS keeps in the build.
+//
+// The body below is the guest code instruction for instruction (each `VOL(x)` is the inlined
+// __MIXGetVolume: x <= -904 -> 0, x >= 60 -> 0xFF64, else the table at 0x802290B0 indexed by x).
+// The registered function reads and writes the CpuContext only through constant indexes; it
+// hands the context to nothing but the checked-mode fallback, which takes it by reference so
+// the translator's contract analysis sees exactly the registers the translation itself uses.
